      "role": "user",
      "content": "The wording for the first section is okay, but I'm a bit worried it might sound too... I don't know, maybe a bit \"mystical\" or like it's just about nature and instinct rather than actual science? \n\nCould we refine it to show that these groups were actually developing complex systematic knowledge, just in a different way? Like, instead of just \"wisdom,\" maybe we can highlight their specific technical mastery or engineering skills so it doesn't sound like they were just living in harmony with nature without actually \"thinking\"? \n\nAlso, for the second section, can we make sure it doesn't sound like the \"modern\" world exists in total isolation from what came before, but still keeps that sense of rapid, logical progress?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
