      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's much better, thanks. I like the use of \"technical mastery\" for the first part. \n\nI just want to double check something for the exhibit flow. When we contrast these two, I want to make sure the visitors understand the *nature* of the difference. \n\nIn the first section, we're looking at these more \"instinctive\" or \"intuitive\" ways of knowing that were tied to their specific environments. But in the second section, we're looking at the transition to a more \"universal\" or \"objective\" way of thinking that allowed for mass industrialization. \n\nCan you write a small transition paragraph that sits between the two sections? I want it to explain how humanity moved from these localized, almost spiritual connections to technology, towards the more detached, analytical, and scalable scientific approach that defines the modern era. It should help justify why we see a jump from the \"old ways\" to the \"civilized\" scientific era.",
